<SiteLayout title="About" description="Why the fictional Southwind team built calmer collaborative operations software.">
  <article class="page-shell py-20 sm:py-28"><div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl"><p class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-primary">About Southwind</p><h1 class="display-title mt-5 text-5xl font-semibold sm:text-6xl">Software should make the work clearer, not become more work.</h1><div class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-lg leading-8 text-muted"><p>Southwind is a fictional collaborative operations product included with Trestle. It demonstrates how a complete, focused SaaS marketing site can connect to an authenticated application without blurring architectural boundaries.</p><p>Its public pages are static Astro source. Authentication, organization membership, billing state, and application behavior stay in the TanStack application and Hono Worker where they belong.</p><p>This content is deliberately easy to replace. Change the centralized identity, rewrite these pages, and make the generated source your own.</p></div></div></article>
</SiteLayout>
